#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.43.7 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:7
msgid ""
"This release includes fixes for CVE-2025-27613, CVE-2025-27614, "
"CVE-2025-46334, CVE-2025-46835, CVE-2025-48384, CVE-2025-48385, and "
"CVE-2025-48386."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.43.6"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:12
msgid "CVE-2025-27613, Gitk:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When a user clones an untrusted repository and runs Gitk without\n"
"additional command arguments, any writable file can be created and\n"
"truncated. The option \"Support per-file encoding\" must have been\n"
"enabled. The operation \"Show origin of this line\" is affected as\n"
"well, regardless of the option being enabled or not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:20
msgid "CVE-2025-27614, Gitk:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Git repository can be crafted in such a way that a user who has\n"
"cloned the repository can be tricked into running any script\n"
"supplied by the attacker by invoking `gitk filename`, where\n"
"`filename` has a particular structure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:27
msgid "CVE-2025-46334, Git GUI (Windows only):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A malicious repository can ship versions of sh.exe or typical\n"
"textconv filter programs such as astextplain. On Windows, path\n"
"lookup can find such executables in the worktree. These programs\n"
"are invoked when the user selects \"Git Bash\" or \"Browse Files\" from\n"
"the menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:35
msgid "CVE-2025-46835, Git GUI:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When a user clones an untrusted repository and is tricked into\n"
"editing a file located in a maliciously named directory in the\n"
"repository, then Git GUI can create and overwrite any writable\n"
"file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:42
msgid "CVE-2025-48384, Git:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When reading a config value, Git strips any trailing carriage\n"
"return and line feed (CRLF). When writing a config entry, values\n"
"with a trailing CR are not quoted, causing the CR to be lost when\n"
"the config is later read.  When initializing a submodule, if the\n"
"submodule path contains a trailing CR, the altered path is read\n"
"resulting in the submodule being checked out to an incorrect\n"
"location. If a symlink exists that points the altered path to the\n"
"submodule hooks directory, and the submodule contains an executable\n"
"post-checkout hook, the script may be unintentionally executed\n"
"after checkout.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:55
msgid "CVE-2025-48385, Git:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When cloning a repository Git knows to optionally fetch a bundle\n"
"advertised by the remote server, which allows the server-side to\n"
"offload parts of the clone to a CDN. The Git client does not\n"
"perform sufficient validation of the advertised bundles, which\n"
"allows the remote side to perform protocol injection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:66
msgid ""
"This protocol injection can cause the client to write the fetched bundle to "
"a location controlled by the adversary. The fetched content is fully "
"controlled by the server, which can in the worst case lead to arbitrary code "
"execution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:68
msgid "CVE-2025-48386, Git:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.43.7.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The wincred credential helper uses a static buffer (`target`) as a\n"
"unique key for storing and comparing against internal storage. This\n"
"credential helper does not properly bounds check the available\n"
"space remaining in the buffer before appending to it with\n"
"`wcsncat()`, leading to potential buffer overflows.\n"
msgstr ""
